*** EMP recovery hotfix 2 ***

Fix HandBrake target-bitrate calculation:

- total_kbps = (target_bytes * 8 * 0.96) / (duration / 1000)
+ total_kbps = (target_bytes * 8 * 0.96) / duration / 1000

The previous expression divided the duration by 1000 before dividing the target bits, inflating the requested kbps by approximately 1,000,000x.

Also retain the last 20 non-empty HandBrake output lines and include them in the raised RuntimeError when HandBrake exits non-zero, so future encoder failures show the actual HandBrake cause instead of only the exit code.

PR trigger: apply verified HF2 patch.
